;; structdef-retirement slice 5 DS-A4 / EF-4: a defstruct field whose type is a
;; built-in compound form with NO runtime value to store in a field is rejected
;; with a clean diagnostic, rather than silently taking the legacy StructDef
;; path.  This keeps the residual StructDef producer path unreachable (the
;; precondition for deleting StructDef).
;;
;; `fn`/`arrow`/`handler` (EF-1/EF-2) and the value-carrying session heads
;; `Session`/`project`/`Role` (EF-4) now lower.  The still-rejected forms are the
;; session PROTOCOL DESCRIPTORS (Send/Recv/Choose/Branch/Rec/Timeout -- type-level
;; only), `Global` (compile-time-only choreography), and `forall` (the EF-3 gate).
;; See docs/archive/history/structdef-exotic-field-forms-plan.md.

(defstruct Cap [h (forall [a] a)])

(defn main [] : int 0)
